<node id="&quot;ERROR HANDLING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Error Handling is a concept involving methods and practices for identifying, managing, and mitigating errors that occur in systems like OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Handling is a methodology described in the guide for dealing with various issues or errors that may arise in the OneStream System."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Handling refers to the methods and practices employed to identify, manage, and rectify errors that occur within the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Handling refers to the process of managing and resolving errors that occur within a system, ensuring smooth operations and integrity of processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Handling refers to the processes and guidelines established within the OneStream system to manage and rectify errors that occur during operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Handling relates to the processes and methodologies applied to address and resolve errors occurring within the OneStream System."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Handling is the process of identifying, managing, and resolving errors occurring in the OneStream system to ensure functionality."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c16dea3c9ee6681708eba0e92091faa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DESCRIPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Description in this context refers to the information outlined in the text about various entities and their relationships."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to a generalized event or situation described in the text, without specifics about attributes or activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description serves as a placeholder, indicating the text being processed but providing no specific details or attributes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to a potential event or context that is not specified in the text provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description is indicated as an event but lacks specific details about its significance or context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description serves as a placeholder in this text, indicating that there is likely an associated narrative or substantive content that isn’t provided in the input."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to the context or background of a situation or narrative, serving as an explanatory note."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to the act of conveying information about a particular subject, and in this context, it signifies the document's potential relevance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to a context or narrative element that is meant to provide further insights or explanations regarding other entities or actions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to an undefined event or context mentioned in the provided text which lacks specific information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to a general overview or representation of information, but lacks specific details or narrative context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to an unspecified event that is central to the context of the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to the event or subject matter being discussed, which encompasses various aspects under consideration in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description is mentioned as an event in the text, but lacks additional context to provide a comprehensive understanding of its attributes or activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to a general concept or an unspecified event that lacks details or context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description is a placeholder text indicating a scenario where information is unspecified but is recognized as an event that may relate to other entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to a detailed representation or account of something, which may encompass various activities, attributes, or characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description is a broad term that can refer to various contexts or narratives within a document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to the contextual information provided in a mapping request that helps clarify the nature of the value in question."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description is a term that refers to an event or a state that outlines or explains something, often serving as a context for further discussion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description is referenced as an event in the context of the document, highlighting the unfolding of events or scenarios."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to a generalized depiction or account of a certain scenario or situation, possibly relevant to specific areas of interest or concern."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to a general outline or representation of some content, lacking specific details."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description serves as a placeholder for the content being analyzed, representing an unspecified event in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term 'Description' is often used to introduce a text or declaration that conveys information about a particular topic or context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to an event that outlines various attributes or a narrative surrounding specific entities or themes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description provides additional context or details about the values or errors encountered during data processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to a generalized representation of content without specific details, implying a placeholder for further information about events or activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description is likely to be a formal entity representing a group or initiative under scrutiny."&lt;SEP&gt;"Description refers to a narrative or summary that presents information about specific entities or contexts within the text."</data>
