ers to a user-specific entity that can be chosen in the dashboard, highlighting the customization aspect of data management."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity refers to any secondary location within the organizational setup that can affect reporting access and data presentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity refers to specific locations associated with individual users, differing from the central entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity refers to a designation within the organizational structure indicating specific user permissions based on their location selection in OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity refers to a specific entity option that can be selected as opposed to a global entity like EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity represents the specific instances or options local to the user's context in the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity refers to an entity that is specific and relevant to the user's local context in the dashboard, different from global entities like EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity is a classification that indicates the user's current base, which differs from the central entity, leading to access issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity refers to a specific organizational unit that users can select for operational purposes in the dashboard."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term 'local entity' refers to a smaller, possibly regional or specific organization or unit as opposed to the global entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity refers to an entity that is specific to a user's context as opposed to a global entity like EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity represents a specific organizational instance that users may be affiliated with, rather than the global framework."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Local Entity is a specific organizational unit that a user is based in, distinct from the Central Entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity refers to a specific entity within the scope of OneStream that may have different permissions and access compared to the central entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity refers to a specific entity that the user selects, distinct from global entities like EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity refers to a specific entity within a localized context, as opposed to a central or global entity, impacting user selection in the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity refers to a regional or specific entity that the user can select instead of the global entity to tailor the data presentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity refers to a specific geographical or operational area where the user is based, distinct from the central entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity refers to any subordinate organization or entity that is not part of the central entity but is involved in the reporting process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity refers to a specific locality where a user is based, contrasting with the central or global entity option."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity refers to the specific entities that users can choose from within their local context as opposed to global options."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity is the point where the related user is based, impacting their access to the P&amp;L MPC report."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity indicates an organization based in a specific geographical area that is relevant for users in their localized context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity refers to an organization that users can select in place of a global entity like EPG_Legal, indicating a localized focus for data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entities are branches or departments that belong to an organization but operate independently from the central entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity represents the specific organization based in the user's region, which should be selected for accurate data processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity refers to a specified organization that users can select from the dashboard for localized data management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity refers to a specific entity that the user can select as opposed to a global entity, indicating a more localized focus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity refers to the entity where the user is based, which prevents them from accessing the central resources like the P&amp;L MPC report."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity refers to organizations that are specific to a user's location and context, as opposed to the central entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity refers to a specific site or subdivision within the larger organization where the user is based, affecting data access under the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity represents specific organizational or geographic entities that users are based in, diverging from the central entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity refers to the entity relevant to the user’s local context, which they can set in the dashboard."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity refers to the organization location where the user is based, affecting their access to reports in OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity signifies the specific organization or entity that the user is associated with, distinct from the central entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Local Entity refers to specific entities that users can select as alternatives to global entities within the dashboard."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity is a specific entity that a user is based in, potentially reflecting a more localized scope of operation in the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity is a designation for an entity that is specific to a certain user, contrasting with the Central Entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity refers to entities relevant to a specific user or context, distinguishing them from global entities like EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity refers to a specific organizational unit from which the user is operating, suggesting limitations in access compared to the central entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity indicates the specific entity associated with the User, which may differ from the Central Entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity refers to the specific subset of the organization where the user is located, affecting their access rights."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity refers to any entity that a user can s