<node id="&quot;CENTRAL USERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Central users are individuals or agents with access privileges to the data of Delivery Hero through EPG_Legal's selection process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who are granted access to entities of Delivery Hero managed by EPG_Legal, playing a key role in data access."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals with elevated access rights who can access data related to Delivery Hero."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users refer to individuals or roles that have privileged access to relevant data within the organization, operating under specific classifications set by EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users refer to individuals who have access to every entity of Delivery Hero as per the legal selection by EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users refer to individuals who have access to every entity of Delivery Hero as per the EPG_Legal selection process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users refer to individuals within the organizational structure of Delivery Hero who have granted access to certain data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users refer to individuals who have the necessary access to entities of Delivery Hero through EPG_Legal's selection process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who have access to all entities of Delivery Hero through EPG_Legal, indicating a privileged role in data access."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who have been granted specific access to data within the organization related to Delivery Hero."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals with authorized access to data from Delivery Hero, playing a critical role in data management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who have specific access privileges to the data managed by EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users refer to individuals who have the authority to access all entities within Delivery Hero, playing a crucial role in data access management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who have unrestricted access to the data handled by EPG_Legal in relation to Delivery Hero."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users refer to a group of individuals who have been granted access to all entities of Delivery Hero, indicating a certain level of authority or privilege in data access."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who have the necessary permissions to access all entities of Delivery Hero, indicating a higher level of access than local users."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who have the authority to access data presented by EPG_Legal in the context of Delivery Hero's selection process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users refer to individuals who have elevated access rights within the EPG_Legal selection process, allowing them to access all entities of Delivery Hero."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals with elevated access who can gain access to entities of Delivery Hero through the EPG_Legal selection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who have the privilege to access legal selections within EPG_Legal related to Delivery Hero."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who have been granted access to data under the current classification system of EPG_Legal, allowing them to view information from Delivery Hero."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who have the necessary classifications to access data presented by EPG_Legal, contrasting with local users."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who have access to every entity of Delivery Hero, indicating a privileged status compared to local users."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users refer to individuals within the organization who have specific permissions to access data related to Delivery Hero, highlighting the hierarchical nature of data access."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who have special access to data within the legal selection process managed by EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are specific individuals granted access to all entities of Delivery Hero through the EPG_Legal selection process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who have the necessary permissions to access all entities presented by EPG_Legal, indicating a specific role in the access mechanism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users are individuals who have specific access rights to entity data within the EPG_Legal system."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d76373bee5d6b8b9e0554f966622cf82</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOCAL USER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A local user is an individual who does not have the necessary classification to access the data presented by EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local user is an individual who does not match the access classification set by EPG_Legal and therefore cannot access relevant data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not match the classification of central users and therefore lack access to relevant data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not match the classification required to access relevant data, thus being restricted from accessing certain information under EPG_Legal protocols."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not possess the necessary classification to access data from Delivery Hero, thereby limiting their access."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not qualify under the classification set by EPG_Legal, thus they cannot access the relevant data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not meet the classification criteria set by EPG_Legal, resulting in their inability to access specific data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not match the classification required to access the relevant data within Delivery Hero."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not match the classification required to access the relevant data from Delivery Hero, highlighting issues of access inequality."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not meet the classification criteria under EPG_Legal, leading to their inability to access relevant data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not match the required classification and therefore cannot access relevant data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not meet the classification criteria set by EPG_Legal, thus lacking access to relevant data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals whose access to data is restricted as they do not meet the classification required by EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals within the organization who do not meet the classification criteria to access certain data, indicating a restricted role."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not match the classification required for accessing relevant data related to Delivery Hero."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not have the same level of access as central users and are unable to access relevant data from Delivery Hero due to their classification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not meet the access classification criteria set by EPG_Legal and thus cannot access relevant data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not match the classification criteria to access data related to Delivery Hero, indicating a limitation in their access rights."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not meet the access classification required by EPG_Legal, limiting their ability to access relevant data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not meet the classification requirements to access the relevant data related to Delivery Hero."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not meet the classification requirements to access relevant data within EPG_Legal and Delivery Hero."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local user refers to individuals who do not meet the classification criteria established by EPG_Legal and therefore cannot access relevant data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local user refers to an individual who does not have access to the relevant data due to classification issues with EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not match the classification for accessing relevant data, illustrating restrictions in data accessibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not meet the criteria for accessing the data managed by EPG_Legal, indicating a restriction in access based on classification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals whose classification does not match with the central users and are therefore restricted from accessing relevant data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not meet the classification criteria to access relevant data as specified by EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local users are individuals who do not have access to certain data within the EPG_Legal framework due to classification issues."</data>
