  <data key="d1">"System denotes the overarching software or platform where entities like User, Central Entity, and Local Entity interact for various functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"System refers to the broader software or framework in which users select entities and experience related issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"System refers to the underlying technology framework that manages entity selections and data display for users."&lt;SEP&gt;"The system represents the overall structure or application that manages the entities and their interactions, ensuring proper functionality."&lt;SEP&gt;"The System is the overarching platform that users interact with for data selection and management, which can include various entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"System typically refers to the overarching software platform, in this context, relating specifically to the OneStream application in question."&lt;SEP&gt;"The System refers to the overarching framework within which entities are selected, suggesting a structured process for user interactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"System refers to the overall technological environment encompassing Okta and OneStream, critical for operational efficiency and user access."&lt;SEP&gt;"System refers to the OneStream System that requires validation and mapping to ensure correct operation."&lt;SEP&gt;"System refers to the overall framework or software platform that users interact with, which manages entity selections and data."&lt;SEP&gt;"The System in this context refers to the OneStream system that is being checked and validated for functionality and accuracy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The System refers to the platform or interface where Users interact and select entities, including EPG_Legal and other entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"System refers to the broader framework or structure within which the transformation rules and validations are applied."</data>
