<node id="&quot;SUPPORT TICKET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Support Ticket is a formal request for assistance raised by a user when encountering errors related to entity access or system performance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Support Ticket is a formal request for help or resolution submitted to the technical support team regarding issues encountered."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support Ticket is an event raised by users when encountering issues, such as 'No Access' error, requiring assistance from the local admin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support Ticket refers to the formal process initiated by users to report problems encountered in the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Support Ticket is an event initiated by a user experiencing issues with the system, indicating the need for technical assistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support Ticket is an action taken by users to report issues or seek assistance regarding system errors or access problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Support Ticket is an event initiated by users encountering issues, allowing them to report problems, such as errors with the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support Ticket is an action taken by users to report issues or errors encountered in the dashboard, often including relevant screenshots."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is an event initiated when users report issues or request assistance regarding the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support ticket is an event where a user reports an issue by submitting a formal request for help regarding access or technical problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support Ticket refers to the action of reporting an issue, such as account access problems, which is part of the operational support process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support Ticket refers to the formal request for assistance that users are advised to raise when they experience issues with the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Support Ticket is an event where users report issues or errors they encounter while using the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is an event where a user raises issues related to access or system errors to receive assistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Support Ticket is an event that users must raise when encountering issues with the OneStream system, allowing users to seek assistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is a formal request for assistance submitted by the user regarding issues related to dashboard access or performance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Support Ticket is an action taken by users to report issues encountered within the OneStream system, requesting assistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is an event raised by users to report issues such as account access problems or system errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is a request raised by users to troubleshoot issues encountered in the system, facilitating prompt assistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is an event created when users report issues, such as errors in access or system performance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Support Ticket is an event where users report issues to OneStream's support team, typically regarding system errors or performance problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is an event initiated by users to request assistance when access issues are encountered."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is a formal request for assistance raised when users encounter issues, such as access problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is an event where users report issues they encounter within the OneStream system, helping track and resolve problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is a formal request raised by a user to seek assistance, typically involving issues encountered during system use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support Ticket is a procedural event initiated when access issues arise, allowing users to report problems and request assistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Support Ticket is an event initiated by users to report issues or errors they encounter while using the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is an event initiated when encountering access issues or system errors, requiring assistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Raising a Support Ticket is an event where users report their issues, specifically regarding access and selection errors encountered."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support Ticket is an action taken by users to report issues they encounter while using the OneStream System, indicating a need for assistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is a request for assistance submitted by users to address problems encountered within the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support Ticket refers to a request raised to seek assistance regarding issues with the dashboard, indicating a troubleshooting process."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is a request for assistance submitted to the support team, typically detailing issues encountered by users of the OneStream System."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support Ticket is a formal request raised by a user to report issues and seek assistance from the technical support team."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is a formal request raised by users to address issues such as access problems or system errors, indicating a need for technical assistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is a formal request raised by users to seek assistance with issues encountered while using the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is an event generated by users when they encounter issues with the OneStream system, often to seek assistance or resolution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support ticket is an event initiated when issues arise, requiring user intervention, such as reporting a problem with access or system errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is raised when issues arise, typically used to request assistance from the local admin regarding access problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket represents an event where users report issues or errors encountered in the OneStream system for resolution."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Support Ticket is an action taken when users encounter issues that require assistance, pointing to a structured process for problem resolution."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is a formal request for assistance submitted by users experiencing issues with the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is an event where users report problems encountered within the OneStream system, to seek resolution for errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support Ticket is an event initiated by users to seek assistance when encountering issues in the system, such as access problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Support Ticket is an event where users report issues or errors related to their account or system access for resolution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support Ticket refers to a formal request for assistance submitted by users reporting issues, such as system errors or performance problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is an event initiated by a user to address issues like access problems in a system."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is an event initiated by users to report issues encountered with the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Support Ticket is an action taken by users to report issues with the OneStream system, involving communication and resolution processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is a request submitted by users to the OneStream organization for assistance in resolving issues encountered in the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support ticket is an event initiated by users when they encounter issues that need resolution, such as account access problems."</data>
