<node id="&quot;ERROR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An error indicates a problem or malfunction that occurs within a system or during a process, requiring troubleshooting to resolve."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error occurs when users encounter messages like 'The system cannot find the file specified' during data import or validation, indicating technical issues with the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error refers to an issue recognized by users while using the OneStream system, particularly during data import, indicating a malfunction in operation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error denotes a malfunction or issue within the OneStream System that requires handling and mapping to rectify."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error indicates a problem encountered during the login process to OneStream, which prevents access to the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error refers to a problem or malfunction that disrupts the normal operation of software or systems, requiring troubleshooting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error refers to the notification indicating 'No Access' for the report presentation, highlighting access restrictions within the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error represents a failure in the login process that prevents users from accessing OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error refers to a presentation failure of the P&amp;L MPC report, indicating issues with data access and visibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error refers to the issue that prevents the successful presentation of the P&amp;L MPC report, specifically reflected as 'No Access' in the report cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error refers to the specific failures encountered during the login process to OneStream, particularly the problems arising from Okta."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error signifies a malfunction or problem occurring within the system that requires user intervention and possibly a support ticket."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error refers to the 'Access Denied' message that users encounter when attempting to log into OneStream, indicating a failure in the authentication process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error refers to the 'No Access' message that users encounter when there are issues with entity assignment or access."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 'Access Denied' error occurs during the login process for OneStream, indicating an issue that prevents users from accessing the platform."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error indicates a problem encountered, specifically the ‘No Access’ issue described, affecting user functionalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error indicates a failure in the authentication process when users try to log into OneStream, resulting in 'Access Denied' messages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error represents a malfunction within the OneStream platform, preventing proper report presentation and signaling 'No Access'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error indicates a problem within the data processing workflow in OneStream, which may arise from unrecognized or unmapped items."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Error refers to a situation experienced by users when trying to log into OneStream, leading to access issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error refers to a malfunction or issue within the system that prevents users from achieving their desired outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error refers to a specific problem encountered during the report presentation, which indicates a failure in the expected functionality."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error represents a failure in the login process, specifically indicating authentication issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error indicates a problem encountered by users when using the OneStream system, specifically related to file importation or validation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b89b929c0b0394b7e9a26ac909ae2f1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-535f01724a527eb2a222ccf841fb81bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c16dea3c9ee6681708eba0e92091faa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de22530deea07aed27df7f24440a6b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20dcb38e4310793f8ff7abda23745bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-978048478f3c25ba13ac704f6f6775ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-468ca5ae82bc8488c43a1095a5da3d74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-974b998f48ab04386086634cf8482ca8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TAB&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tab indicates a specific section of the dashboard that requires refreshing to apply changes made by the user."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Tab signifies a user interface element in the dashboard that must be refreshed after selecting a new entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tab is a feature in the user interface that users refresh to apply changes made in entity selections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tab refers to the interface component that needs to be refreshed for changes to be applied in the dashboard."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tab refers to a section of the dashboard that needs to be refreshed after changes are made to update the data presentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tab represents an interactive element within the dashboard that needs to be refreshed for changes to take effect."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tab refers to the action of refreshing the dashboard to apply changes made to the entity selection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tab represents a functional part of the dashboard that requires refreshing to apply changes made by the user."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tab refers to a navigational element within the dashboard that users interact with to make changes related to entity selection and data presentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tab represents a section in the dashboard interface that needs to be refreshed after making changes to ensure updated data is presented."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tab refers to a section within the dashboard where users can make selections or changes related to entity management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tab is a part of the dashboard interface that allows users to refresh and apply changes after selection of entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tab refers to a section of the dashboard that can be refreshed to apply changes made by the user."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tab is an action taken by the user in the dashboard interface to refresh and apply changes made to the entity selections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9ff29e8a6836503d6ce44b763aa795c9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GLOBAL ENTITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Global Entity refers to broader entity options like EPG_Legal that are available in the Entity Selector."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Global Entity represents a larger organizational unit that encompasses various local entities, influencing user selections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Global entity refers to entities like EPG_Legal that are recognized universally across the dashboard interface."&lt;SEP&gt;"Global Entity refers to universally recognized entities that can be accessed by all users within the dashboard environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Global Entity represents a classification within the system that is different from Local Entity and Central Entity, indicating a broader or overarching organizational structure."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9ff29e8a6836503d6ce44b763aa795c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d67c1dc051ea34b153886bca7e68844</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Account is a category within the data model that organizes financial transactions in accounting systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a category or financial entity within the OneStream platform used for financial reporting and analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a financial account in the OneStream system that is used for various accounting purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to stored data entries in the systems such as SAP, Dynamics, or OneStream that need to be kept consistent across platforms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to the user profile associated with the individual, which must be correctly assigned to access the organization's resources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account represents user profiles that require correct entity assignments within the organizational structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to user profiles that grant permissions and access within the dashboard system, tied to specific entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to the user's credentials and permissions linked to the dashboard for accessing different entities and functionalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"An account refers to a record in financial software systems that can have discrepancies affecting data validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Accounts are identifiers for financial transactions and data entries that require accurate mapping between different software systems to ensure consistency."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a record in a financial system that stores information about transactions, balances, and entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a structural element in financial data management that categorizes transactions, often utilized within platforms like OneStream for financial reporting."&lt;SEP&gt;"An account represents a record in financial data management that OneStream processes and maps to provide insights."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a financial account that is involved in the data import process within the OneStream data model, which can lead to validation errors if not correctly handled."&lt;SEP&gt;"An account refers to a record or representation of data that is processed and managed within OneStream's system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a financial entry in accounting that plays a role in the data validation process within OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Account in this context refers to a record containing financial or operational information that requires mapping between different systems like SAP, Dynamics, and OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"An account in this context refers to a user representation or related data item that may require mapping within OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"An account refers to a financial entity or account in OneStream where user-defined members have specific rules for access and validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a financial record or entry that tracks the balance of various transactions within the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a user profile or data entry that is being managed within the OneStream platform, where it may encounter mapping issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a user profile or record within the OneStream system that can become unrecognized."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account represents a financial or data storage unit used within OneStream for tracking and reporting transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a financial account used in accounting, which is important for financial reporting and analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a unit of financial data in the OneStream system that requires recognition and mapping to function correctly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to financial records tracked in OneStream, essential for data import and financial reporting."&lt;SEP&gt;"The account refers to the user profile that must be assigned correctly to access particular entities on the dashboard."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a specific financial record within OneStream that can be categorized as either intercompany or non-intercompany."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to financial records maintained in systems like SAP, Dynamics, and OneStream, crucial for financial management."&lt;SEP&gt;"An account refers to a record or entry that is part of financial data within the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a financial record that is integral to the OneStream data model, categorizing transactions and balances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a user or data item that may be affected by the mapping errors in OneStream, indicating potential discrepancies in data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to the financial records that track assets, liabilities, equity, revenue, and expenses, crucial for monitoring an organization's financial health."&lt;SEP&gt;"An account refers to a financial representation used within OneStream, which can be subject to recognition issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a financial account used in reporting that may contain data related to various transactions and balances."&lt;SEP&gt;"An account is a record that holds financial information and is utilized within OneStream for data management."&lt;SEP&gt;"An account refers to a user or system record that is maintained within financial or operational software systems such as SAP or Dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to an instance or entity within OneStream where user-defined members are mapped and validated based on certain rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Account refers to a financial record kept within OneStream that may be new or unrecognized during data processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account refers to a financial record used in accounting and finance; it is fundamental to tracking and reporting financial transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"An account in OneStream refers to a specific entity that has rules and mappings associated with user-defined members for validation purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"An account is a record or item within a financial or operational system that may require mapping for proper identification and reporting."&lt;SEP&gt;"An account refers to the user profile that is assigned to a specific entity, determining the level of access and permissions within the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"An account represents a record in financial systems that tracks transactions and balances for a specific entity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c686046d60abc94ecd48dc9fcb9279e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89b929c0b0394b7e9a26ac909ae2f1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16b8771a1ab8fe5a7c40a0d7f824295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea39b0642b07a482ff2bcf0a453bb06f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-974b998f48ab04386086634cf8482ca8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ERROR MESSAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Error Message is a notification displayed to users indicating a problem, such as 'The system cannot find the file specified,' often leading to user actions like raising support tickets."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Error Message is an event that occurs when the system cannot find the specified file, indicating a problem with the data import process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message indicates that users are experiencing access issues, prompting checks and troubleshooting steps."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message is a notification that appears when a problem occurs during the operation of the OneStream system, indicating issues such as file accessibility or connectivity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message refers to notifications displayed to users when issues arise during data import or validation in the OneStream system, indicating that the system cannot find the specified file."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error message 'Access Denied' indicates a failure in authentication during the login process to OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message such as 'No Access' indicates a problem with user access rights that needs to be addressed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error message is a notification displayed to users indicating a failure to authenticate during the OneStream login process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message is a notification generated by OneStream indicating issues with data imports or mappings that need to be resolved."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error messages occur when there are issues in the OneStream system, indicating problems like file not being found during data import."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message indicates issues that arise when an account or item from source data is not recognized by OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message is a notification generated by OneStream indicating that something is wrong, specifically related to unrecognized values."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message is a notification received by users indicating issues like 'The system cannot find the file specified,' signaling a problem with the operation being performed."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message indicates an issue with unrecognized items in the source data, signaling a need for attention in the mapping process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message refers to the notification displayed when access is denied, indicating a problem with user permissions or settings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message represents the notification seen by users when they fail to log into OneStream, signaling an issue with authentication."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error message is a communication sent by OneStream that indicates issues encountered during data validation or interoperability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message is a notification generated by OneStream indicating issues with data import, providing details about unrecognized source values."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error message indicates a situation where an account or item from source data is unrecognized, signaling a problem in data mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error message provides feedback about validation issues, indicating which dimension is missing or invalid."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message indicates an issue that arises during data import, signaling that there is a problem with the data structure or mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error message refers to a notification indicating that some data is unrecognized or not mapped in the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Error Message is a notification that indicates missing or invalid dimensions, guiding users on how to address issues in the validation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message is a notification that indicates an issue, such as a missing dimension, that needs to be resolved during data validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error message indicates an issue with data mapping that alerts users to problems with unspecified source values."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error message is the notification received when a validation fails, which indicates issues in data import related to the OneStream model."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message is a notification that alerts users to issues in the data validation process, indicating missing or invalid dimensions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Error Message indicates a problem where a source value is new or unrecognized within the OneStream system, highlighting issues in data mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message is a notification displayed to users when issues occur within the OneStream system, indicating the system cannot find the specified file."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message is a notification generated by the system indicating that there is an issue with data mapping or recognition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message is a notification that indicates issues with data validation, specifically highlighting missing or invalid dimensions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message refers to the notification received by users indicating that access has been denied, preventing them from logging in."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error messages are alerts generated by OneStream when an import fails due to incorrect data configurations or mappings."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message like 'The system cannot find the file specified' is displayed to users indicating problems during data operations in the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message refers to a notification indicating that there is an unrecognized source value in OneStream, signaling an issue that needs resolution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error message provides information about missing or invalid dimensions during validation, guiding corrective actions."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message is a notification that indicates a problem has occurred, in this case related to the IDX10222 error encountered by users."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message is a notification that indicates there is an issue with mapping data in OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message is a notification provided by OneStream that helps identify issues with data import, including which source value is unrecognized."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message refers to the notification indicating a missing dimension that aids in identifying issues during validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message is a notification about issues or unrecognized values encountered by OneStream during data mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message refers to notifications generated when a data record fails validation due to issues like missing or invalid dimensions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error message refers to notifications generated by OneStream that indicate problems with data import or validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Error Message is an alert produced by OneStream when it encounters unrecognized or new items in the source data."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message is an indication that something has gone wrong in the system, such as the Token / Time Synchronization Error (IDX10222)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message refers to the notification shown to users when they are denied access to OneStream, indicating a failure in the login process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error message indicates which dimensions are missing or invalid, guiding users in troubleshooting data validation issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"An error message is a notification indicating an issue with data mapping or recognition within OneStream, often providing specific information about unrecognized values."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message conveys information about an issue encountered during the data import process in OneStream, indicating what is wrong."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message describes the issue users encounter when trying to log in to OneStream via Okta, suggesting synchronization problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message is a notification indicating missing or invalid dimensions during the validation process, prompting users to troubleshoot."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error Message is the notification displayed to users when a login attempt fails, indicating the specific reason for the access denial."&lt;SEP&gt;"Error message is a notification displayed to users indicating issues during their login process to OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error message 'Access Denied' signifies the problem encountered by users during the login process to OneStream."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce0780d24064345ea48452ca4fdab2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89b929c0b0394b7e9a26ac909ae2f1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-535f01724a527eb2a222ccf841fb81bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16b8771a1ab8fe5a7c40a0d7f824295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20dcb38e4310793f8ff7abda23745bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6b60420ea1af607508cb6e918ae83d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-468ca5ae82bc8488c43a1095a5da3d74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40bb20380c8b404567120c05e612b932&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60f6d19de7358e3edd06cf31c15732a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-974b998f48ab04386086634cf8482ca8</data>
</node>
