<node id="&quot;VIDEO CALLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Video Calls are a form of communication where participants can see and hear each other using video technology, often consuming significant bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Video Calls are live communications conducted over the internet that may consume significant bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Video Calls are live visual interactions facilitated by internet connectivity, often consuming significant bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Video calls are events where visual and audio communication occurs between participants via the internet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Video calls are real-time audio-visual communications conducted over the internet, which can be bandwidth-intensive."&lt;SEP&gt;"Video Calls are communications made over the internet that can consume significant bandwidth, impacting overall connection performance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Video Calls are real-time visual communication sessions conducted over the internet, often heavy on bandwidth requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Video Calls are real-time communications between individuals using video technology, often requiring substantial internet bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Video Calls are live, visual communications conducted over the internet, often requiring significant bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Video calls are a method of communication that uses video technology for real-time visual interaction over the internet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Video Calls are events where users engage in real-time visual communication over the internet, often consuming significant bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Video Calls are real-time visual communication sessions conducted over the internet, which can consume significant bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Video Calls are online communication events that utilize video and audio to connect users, potentially consuming significant bandwidth."</data>
