<node id="&quot;STREAMING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Streaming is an event where multimedia content is transmitted over the internet, requiring considerable bandwidth for smooth playback."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streaming refers to the continuous transmission of audio or video files over the internet, which can also use heavy bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streaming refers to the continuous transmission of audio or video content over the internet, which uses substantial bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streaming refers to the continuous transmission of media over the internet, which can also utilize heavy bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streaming is the delivery of audio, video, or other media over the internet in real time, requiring substantial bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streaming refers to the transmission of audio or video data over the internet in real-time, which requires a stable internet connection and bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streaming refers to the continuous transmission of audio or video content over the internet, usually requiring high bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streaming refers to the continuous transmission of audio or video files over the internet, which can consume significant bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streaming refers to a method of transmitting or receiving data over the internet in a continuous flow, typically involving audio or video content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streaming refers to the continuous transmission of audio or video files over the internet, requiring substantial bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streaming refers to the continuous transmission of audio or video content over the internet, which can also use considerable bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streaming refers to the continuous delivery of audio or video content over the internet, often requiring substantial bandwidth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streaming is the continuous transmission of audio or video files over the internet, which can also use heavy bandwidth."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-978048478f3c25ba13ac704f6f6775ca</data>
</node>
