  <data key="d1">"Unstable Wi-Fi denotes a fluctuating wireless internet service that can disrupt cloud application performance, particularly during data transfers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unstable Wi-Fi refers to a type of internet connection characterized by variability in connectivity, which can affect cloud-based applications like OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unstable Wi-Fi refers to a poor internet connection that can disrupt data transfer processes in cloud applications, leading to failures in operations."</data>
