<node id="&quot;VALIDATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Validation involves checking or confirming the integrity and correctness of the data being imported into OneStream, crucial for smooth operation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is an event that occurs during data processing when the system checks the accuracy and completeness of data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the event where OneStream assesses data input for compatibility and accuracy, potentially leading to errors if issues arise."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking data for accuracy and completeness within the OneStream system, where users may experience issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking data or inputs for accuracy and completeness, often necessary during data import processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation refers to the process of ensuring that the data or system is correct and meets the required standards or formats."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking if the input data meets certain criteria before it is processed or imported into a system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of confirming data integrity when importing it into OneStream, potentially interrupted by errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking whether the input data meets certain criteria or mappings within a system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process by which OneStream verifies if the values in a file can be correctly mapped to its members."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking if data meets certain criteria or requirements, ensuring correctness before proceeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process in OneStream that checks for proper mapping and verifies data integrity before proceeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation refers to the process of checking the integrity and accuracy of data, which may be impacted during technical errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation refers to the process of ensuring that account values are consistent and correctly mapped across various software systems, preventing errors in financial reporting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking whether the input data meets the required standards and criteria before proceeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of ensuring that data is accurate and consistent across different systems to avoid mismatches."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation refers to the process of checking data correctness and compliance with the rules of the OneStream data model."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of ensuring that the data adheres to the set transformation rules and is consistent across different systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation refers to the process where systems check data for accuracy and completeness, ensuring that inputs match expected formats or parameters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking the correctness of combinations of user-defined members in OneStream to ensure they conform to set rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking the correctness of data in the mapping to ensure all needed dimensions are present."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation refers to the process of checking data against predefined criteria to ensure its accuracy and integrity during financial reporting or data integration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is an event that occurs to check for correctness and completeness of data before processing or use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is an event that occurs within the context of data processing, ensuring that data entries meet required formats and mappings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking the accuracy and compliance of the data being imported into OneStream against its data model."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process that checks whether the dimensions in a record are correctly paired and valid according to defined rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is an event that entails checking the accuracy and proper functioning of mappings or processes within the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking the accuracy and completeness of the data being mapped, ensuring all required dimensions are included."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of ensuring that data is correct, accurate, and meets the required standards before it can be used in workflows."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation refers to the process within the OneStream system where users ensure that data imports meet specified criteria before proceeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking data against specified criteria to ensure its accuracy and completeness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of ensuring that data is correct, accurate, and adheres to the specified rules or maps, crucial for data integrity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of verifying the accuracy and correctness of data within the OneStream System."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation refers to the process of assessing the correctness and alignment of data and systems, crucial in ensuring accurate output from OneStream and Excel."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking data against a set of standards or criteria, often to ensure accuracy or correctness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking that the data meets the criteria necessary for successful mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking whether the system's functionalities and transformations are correct and as expected."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation refers to the process of checking data to ensure it meets certain criteria before being processed, which can lead to errors if not aligned correctly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation refers to the process of verifying and ensuring that data or systems meet required standards and specifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking and confirming the accuracy and correctness of formulations within the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of checking data for accuracy and completeness, ensuring that all necessary elements are present before processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Validation is the process of confirming that the data in the OneStream system and Excel is ac