<node id="&quot;SOURCE FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A source file is the original data input that is utilized in OneStream for mapping user-defined members and ensuring accurate validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File is the original data file from which values are extracted and need to be mapped to OneStream members."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file contains data that is submitted for validation and mapping within the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File refers to the original file containing data that is being imported or processed by the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Source File is the data file that is being validated and may include values that need to be mapped to OneStream members."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file is the document that contains data which undergoes validation and potential corrections during the mapping process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file is a location within the data structure where original data is stored and may be subject to corrections."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file is the document or data set that contains the dimensions which need to be checked for validation in OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File refers to the original data file being used for validation in the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Source File is a document or dataset utilized in the mapping process that contains essential information for validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Source File is the location where data dimensions should be provided and checked against the requirements for validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file is the original data file that may contain incorrect user-defined member assignments leading to validation failures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File refers to the original data file from which user-defined members and their mappings are derived, playing a key role in data uploads."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file is a document or data set used as the original input for mapping, which may affect the outcome if incorrect."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file is the original document where data dimensions should be provided for validation in OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"A source file is the original document or dataset that contains data needing validation and potential dimensional mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file contains the data that is used for mapping user-defined members in OneStream and must be correct to avoid validation issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file is a document from which data is extracted for mapping. It must contain the correct UD for successful validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File refers to the document where the data dimensions are initially provided for validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File refers to the original data input from which mappings are created, essential for accurate data processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File represents the initial data being processed in OneStream, which may contain values needing mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file contains the data that is being validated, where dimensions should be present for successful processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file is a document used as input for the mapping process, which may contain various data fields."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File is the location where the data is stored, which is checked for the presence of required dimensions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source file refers to the original data file being used in the mapping process, which can contain various dimensions that need to be correctly configured."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File is the document or file being used that may contain incorrect data leading to mapping errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File is the origin from which data dimensions are retrieved and checked for validity in the validation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source file refers to the original file being uploaded or processed in OneStream, which may contain values requiring mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File is a file used in the context of data processing that may contain the incorrect UD leading to mapping errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File refers to the file containing data that needs to be mapped to valid OneStream members, essential for system functionality."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source file is the original data file that contains the UD members and which may contain errors that need correction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source file refers to the location where data is stored, which is checked to validate the presence of required dimensions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File is a document or dataset that contains the data needing to be mapped according to the defined parameters and dimensions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source File is the location where data records originate and are checked for required dimensions before validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Source file is the file from which values are being mapped to OneStream members, playing a significant role in triggering mapping errors."</data>
