<node id="&quot;ROOT CAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Root Cause is a concept referring to the underlying issue that arises when personal Excel documentations do not align with the expected format."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to an underlying issue that affects the mapping of account values in various systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the fundamental issue leading to validation failures in data integration between OneStream, SAP, and Dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the fundamental issue that leads to errors in data validation, emphasizing the need for thorough mapping rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the underlying issue that affects the validation process when integrating different systems such as SAP, Dynamics, and OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the fundamental reason for an issue, particularly relating to data mapping and validation failures in business software systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the underlying problem that leads to a failure in mapping rules between systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the underlying issue that leads to validation failures in data mapping among different systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the primary issue related to mapping rules in the context of data integration and validation failures amongst various systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the underlying issues or problems that arise during the mapping and validation process between different software applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the identification of primary issues in data mapping and validation processes that can lead to errors or discrepancies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the underlying reason for discrepancies in mapping and validation processes across various financial systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the underlying issue that leads to validation failures in the mapping process between different financial systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root cause refers to the underlying issue that affects data presentation and alignment between OneStream and Excel."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the underlying issue that leads to discrepancies in financial account mapping and validation processes across different systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root cause refers to the underlying issue or reason for a problem, in this case, related to document formatting and integration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the underlying issues or problems in the system that lead to validation failures in data mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Root Cause refers to the identification of underlying issues that lead to validation failures between different software systems."</data>
