<node id="&quot;DYNAMICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dynamics refers to Microsoft Dynamics, a line of enterprise resource planning and customer relationship management software applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to a suite of enterprise resource planning and customer relationship management applications developed by Microsoft."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to Microsoft Dynamics, a suite of enterprise resource planning (ERP) and customer relationship management (CRM) software applications that require data consistency with other systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to a suite of enterprise resource planning and customer relationship management applications that are part of Microsoft."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to Microsoft's Dynamics software, which is used for business management and financial processes, affecting account validation and mapping rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to Microsoft Dynamics, a suite of enterprise resource planning (ERP) and customer relationship management (CRM) software applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics, commonly known as Microsoft Dynamics, is a suite of enterprise resource planning (ERP) and customer relationship management (CRM) software applications that must coordinate with OneStream for effective data handling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to Microsoft Dynamics, a suite of business applications for enterprise resource planning (ERP) and customer relationship management (CRM)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to a suite of enterprise resource planning (ERP) and customer relationship management (CRM) software applications developed by Microsoft."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to Microsoft Dynamics, a suite of enterprise resource planning and customer relationship management applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to Microsoft Dynamics, a suite of business applications that aid in customer relationship management and enterprise resource planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to a suite of intelligent business applications provided by Microsoft for managing business processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to Microsoft Dynamics, a suite of enterprise resource planning applications for business management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to Microsoft Dynamics, a suite of business applications integrated with accounting and financial management functions, which can also affect validation outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to Microsoft Dynamics, a suite of enterprise resource planning and customer relationship management applications designed for businesses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to a suite of enterprise resource planning and customer relationship management applications offered by Microsoft."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to Microsoft Dynamics, a suite of enterprise resource planning and customer relationship management applications used by businesses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamics refers to Microsoft Dynamics, a suite of enterprise resource planning (ERP) and customer relationship management (CRM) software applications."</data>
