<node id="&quot;WORKFLOW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The workflow represents the sequence of processes or steps followed in data handling and validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow is a systematic series of steps or processes carried out to achieve a specific task or outcome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow is the sequence of processes through which data is processed and validated, emphasizing the importance of correct data mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to the structured series of processes and steps that guide how data is handled and transformed within the application."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow represents a sequence of processes or steps that are designed to accomplish a specific task or function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to the sequence of processes through which data is handled, including the application of transformation rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow represents the series of processes or tasks that need to be followed for proper validation and mapping in the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to a series of processes or tasks that are implemented to achieve a specific goal or output in a structured manner."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to the systematic process followed within the application or platform to handle data processing and validation operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow represents a systematic process used to carry out tasks, in this case involving profiles and validations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to the sequence of processes involved in the Application where data is handled, validated, and transformed according to specific rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to the sequence of processes through which a piece of work passes from initiation to completion, including validation and mapping steps."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to the sequence of processes through which a piece of work passes from initiation to completion, essential for managing tasks in a project."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow represents the systematic process or sequence of steps involved in data handling or operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to the established processes or systems used to manage the data transformation and validation activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to the process by which data is managed and moved through the various systems in an organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to the sequence of processes or steps that are executed in handling data, which may include validation and mapping tasks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow in this context refers to the predefined processes that guide how data is handled and validated across different systems like OneStream, SAP, and Dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to the sequence of processes or steps through which data is managed, which can influence how rules are applied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow represents a sequence of processes or steps taken to manage tasks and ensure correct mapping and validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to a structured sequence of processes or activities designed to accomplish a particular task or project in the context of mapping and validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to a defined process or system of operation within which tasks are executed and validated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to the sequence of processes or tasks involved in data handling, ensuring proper execution of transformation rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to the sequence of processes or tasks through which a piece of work passes from initiation to completion in a system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow refers to the series of processes or rules being followed within the Application to handle data validation and transformations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workflow represents the sequence of processes or tasks that must be executed to achieve a desired outcome, crucial for proper functioning."</data>
