  <data key="d1">"P&amp;L (Profit and Loss) account refers to financial accounts that summarize revenues and expenses, which play a role in data import validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"P&amp;L Account refers to a Profit and Loss account that tracks revenues and expenses in financial reporting."&lt;SEP&gt;"P&amp;L Account stands for Profit and Loss Account, a type of account used in financial reporting to summarize revenues and expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"P&amp;L account refers to Profit and Loss accounts in financial reporting, which must be correctly mapped to avoid validation errors in OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"P&amp;L Account refers to profit and loss accounts that are affected by the rules and conditions of data import within OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"P&amp;L account represents profit and loss accounts used in financial reporting to summarize revenues and expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"P&amp;L account stands for profit and loss account, which summarizes the revenues, costs, and expenses incurred during a specific period."&lt;SEP&gt;"P&amp;L account refers to profit and loss accounts used in financial reporting within OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"P&amp;L account refers to profit and loss accounts which are critical in financial reporting and must adhere to data model rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"P&amp;L account refers to profit and loss accounts in financial reporting that summarize revenues and expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"P&amp;L Account refers to a type of financial account focusing on profit and loss within the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"P&amp;L account refers to profit and loss accounts that summarize revenues and expenses for a specific period, essential for understanding financial performance."&lt;SEP&gt;"P&amp;L account represents the profit and loss account in an accounting system where financial performance is measured."&lt;SEP&gt;"P&amp;L Account, or Profit and Loss Account, is a financial statement that summarizes revenues, costs, and expenses to show net profit or loss over a period."</data>
