<node id="&quot;OS SUPPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"OS Support is an organization referenced in the context of providing technical assistance for fixing mapping errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS Support is an organization responsible for providing technical assistance and resolving issues related to mapping errors within the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support is an organization that provides assistance in resolving mapping issues related to dimensions and file corrections."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support refers to the support team associated with OneStream, responsible for resolving issues related to user-defined member validations and mappings."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support refers to the support team responsible for addressing issues related to the OneStream application."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support is an organization that provides technical support for mapping issues and corrections in the validation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support refers to the support team responsible for addressing issues arising from the OneStream software, assisting users with validation failures and configuration mistakes."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support refers to the support team within the OneStream organization that helps resolve issues related to invalid mappings and combinations."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS Support is the team responsible for addressing issues related to invalid combinations in OneStream's data mappings and file uploads."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support is an organization responsible for providing technical assistance and fixing mapping-related issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support is an organization that provides technical assistance and fixes for issues related to the mapping process and validation errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support refers to the support team responsible for fixing issues related to OneStream's mapping and validation failures."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS Support is an organizational entity that provides technical support and assistance related to system mapping and validation issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support refers to the support team handling issues related to OneStream, tasked with resolving mapping validation failures."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS Support is the support team designated to assist with issues regarding mapping failures and invalid combinations in OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support refers to the organizational support team responsible for fixing mapping issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support is an organization that provides assistance with mapping issues and validations in the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support is the support team responsible for resolving issues related to mapping and validation failures within OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support is the organization responsible for providing assistance and fixing issues related to mapping errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support refers to the support team associated with OneStream, responsible for assisting with issues related to mapping and user-defined combinations."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support is a service associated with OneStream that assists in resolving issues related to invalid data combinations and mapping errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS Support is an organizational entity responsible for troubleshooting and correcting mapping issues as presented in the context."&lt;SEP&gt;"OS support is the support team associated with OneStream, responsible for assisting users with issues related to mappings and validation failures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea39b0642b07a482ff2bcf0a453bb06f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76aa6c22f3802deaded720e799800d74</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"UD (User Defined) refers to custom fields or identifiers in the mapping process that must be correctly set to avoid errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD (user-defined) refers to customizable members within OneStream accounts that dictate how data is structured and validated."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD (user-defined) refers to specific members or values that are defined by users within the OneStream system, which must adhere to specific rules for account validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD refers to the User Definition, which is used in the context of data mapping and validation process in systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD, or User Defined dimensions, are custom dimensions that can be created in OneStream to meet specific reporting needs."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD is a dimension in the OneStream data model which represents a specific type of financial data or transaction context."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD stands for User Defined, which represents specific identifiers or dimensions that are necessary for mapping in the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD (user-defined) refers to specific members within OneStream accounts that are subject to validation rules and mappings."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD refers to a specific dimension in OneStream that is combined with Accounts but is not allowed in certain import scenarios."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD refers to the unique designator used in the mapping process that must be correct for validation to succeed."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD refers to a unique identifier or code used in the mapping process to ensure data integrity and proper associations between records."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD (User Defined) represents specific identifiers used in the context of mapping that must be correctly utilized to avoid errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD (user-defined) refers to a customizable attribute or member that users can define within OneStream for account management and validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD refers to a uniform descriptor used in data mapping processes, which must be correctly applied to avoid errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD stands for user-defined, representing custom members that define rules within the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD refers to a unique identifier or business line required for proper mapping in systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD is an event indicating the identification of a Universal Dimension required for proper mapping in a data system."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD refers to a specific type of dimension that can be used for reporting in the OneStream application."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD (User-Defined) refers to the custom-defined attributes or members for accounts in OneStream that dictate which combinations are valid."&lt;SEP&gt;"UD refers to the user-defined dimension used in the context of mapping and data validation, essential for ensuring the correct combination of data."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e16b8771a1ab8fe5a7c40a0d7f824295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea39b0642b07a482ff2bcf0a453bb06f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76aa6c22f3802deaded720e799800d74</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CUBE VIEW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cube View is a feature within the OneStream platform that displays valid combinations for accounts and assists in troubleshooting mapping issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cube View is an event or action that involves examining valid combinations of mappings for accounts in OneStream, used for troubleshooting validation issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cube View is a visual representation in OneStream that displays valid combinations for accounts, assisting users in resolving mapping issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cube View refers to a feature or event within the OneStream environment used to visualize valid combinations for accounts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cube View refers to a feature in OneStream that allows users to see valid combinations for accounts, playing a critical role in troubleshooting issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cube View is a specific view within OneStream used to display valid combinations for accounts and user-defined members."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cube View is an action taken to examine valid combinations for accounts during the validation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cube View refers to a user interface in OneStream that displays valid combinations for accounts, helping users troubleshoot mapping issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cube View is an event or action that allows users to view valid combinations for accounts and their mappings within the OneStream software."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cube View is an event or process within OneStream that allows users to view valid combinations for account mappings, facilitating error resolution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cube View is an event or action taken to review valid combinations for accounts within OneStream for troubleshooting purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cube View is an event or process in OneStream used to display valid combinations for accounts based on user-defined members."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea39b0642b07a482ff2bcf0a453bb06f</data>
</node>
