  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intercompany Partner is an organization that may be affected by mapping errors related to required dimension combinations in a system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intercompany Partner refers to an individual or entity involved in a business relationship, specifically needing proper dimensions for mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intercompany Partner refers to an individual or entity involved in business transactions between different companies, which plays a role in the mapping process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intercompany Partner refers to an organization that is involved in a collaborative or contractual relation between companies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intercompany Partner refers to an individual or entity involved in business arrangements between different companies and is relevant in the context of mapping errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intercompany Partner refers to an organization involved in cross-company dealings or collaborations, implying a multi-organizational relationship within the mapping context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intercompany Partner is an organizational entity involved in a business context, requiring proper dimensional combinations for mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intercompany Partner refers to an individual or entity involved in business relationships between companies, specifically in the context of mapping data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intercompany Partner refers to a partner or entity involved in intercompany transactions that may require correct mapping for validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intercompany Partner refers to an entity involved in business transactions that may have mapping and validation requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intercompany Partner refers to a business entity involved in intercompany transactions, whose valid combinations are essential for system operations."</data>
