<node id="&quot;DIMENSION COMBINATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dimension Combinations are specific groupings of data requirements that must be fulfilled for successful validation in the mapping process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension combinations refer to the necessary groupings of data fields required for proper validation in data mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension combinations refer to the pairing of different dimensions in a record that must be valid for the record to pass validation in OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension combinations refer to the various required data elements that need to be linked or matched for accurate mapping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension combinations refer to specific pairings of dimensions that are required for data records to pass validation in OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension combinations refer to the unique sets of attributes or parameters that need to be aligned during the mapping process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension combinations refer to specific groupings of attributes in the data that are needed for validation, without which errors may occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension Combinations represent the various configurations of attributes required for effective data modeling and validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension combinations refer to the necessary pairings of data attributes that must be validated together for data integrity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension combinations refer to the various pairs of attributes that must be correctly aligned in mapping to prevent errors during validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension combinations refer to the specific groupings of data elements that OneStream enforces to ensure valid records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension Combinations refer to the specific pairings or set of data attributes needed for successful mapping and validation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76aa6c22f3802deaded720e799800d74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6b60420ea1af607508cb6e918ae83d8</data>
</node>
