<node id="&quot;TOKENS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tokens are secure authentication elements used by OneStream that are time-sensitive and necessary for user login."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a57c6b9afbd15940a292bd5d99564c9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SYSTEM CLOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"System Clock refers to the built-in clock of the local computer that must be synchronized with the server time for valid authentication."&lt;SEP&gt;"System Clock refers to the timing mechanism of the Local Computer that must be synchronized with a server to ensure valid authentication tokens."&lt;SEP&gt;"System Clock represents the internal timekeeping mechanism of the local computer which must be correctly synchronized to validate authentication tokens."&lt;SEP&gt;"The system clock refers to the internal clock of a computer that keeps track of the current time and is essential for validating authentication tokens."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a57c6b9afbd15940a292bd5d99564c9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SERVER TIME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Server Time is the authoritative reference time used by OneStream to validate authentication tokens against the Local Computer's time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Server Time is the reference time against which the local computer's system clock is synchronized to ensure valid token authentication."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a57c6b9afbd15940a292bd5d99564c9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIME UPDATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Time Updates are automatic updates that adjust the Local Computer's system clock to maintain synchronization with server time, crucial for token validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Time Updates refer to the automatic adjustments that synchronize the local computer's clock with the server time, ensuring the validity of authentication tokens."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a57c6b9afbd15940a292bd5d99564c9</data>
</node>
