</node>
<node id="&quot;SERVER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A server is a specialized computer used in the Internet Time synchronization process to provide accurate time data for client computers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Server is the backend system that validates authentication tokens based on its system time, interacting with the local computer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A server provides time synchronization for computers through Internet Time synchronization, ensuring accurate timekeeping."&lt;SEP&gt;"A server refers to a computer or system that provides data, resources, or services to other computers, used for time synchronization in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Server refers to a networked machine that provides data and synchronization services to client machines, critical for maintaining accurate time and functionality."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce0780d24064345ea48452ca4fdab2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a57c6b9afbd15940a292bd5d99564c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7f61d30a0ba8c3e8f0c330fd9e6d495</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTHENTICATION TOKENS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Authentication Tokens are time-sensitive codes used for securing user access in the OneStream login process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a57c6b9afbd15940a292bd5d99564c9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERNET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Internet is the network that connects the local computer to the server, crucial for updating system time automatically."&lt;SEP&gt;"The internet is the global network that connects computers and enables the synchronization of system clocks among devices, crucial for authentication."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a57c6b9afbd15940a292bd5d99564c9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATE AND TIME SETTINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Date and Time settings are a feature on computers that allow users to adjust time-related parameters like time automatic settings and time zones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Date and Time settings are a series of adjustments on a computer that ensure the clock displays the correct local time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Date and Time settings refer to the configurations on a computer that determine the system's clock settings and timezone."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7f61d30a0ba8c3e8f0c330fd9e6d495</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPUTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A computer is a device that users interact with to access applications like OneStream, requiring proper settings for functionality."&lt;SEP&gt;"A computer is the device on which the Date and Time settings are adjusted and from which users access OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"Computer refers to the device being used to access settings and run applications, playing a central role in the process described."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7f61d30a0ba8c3e8f0c330fd9e6d495</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIME ZONE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
