<edge source="&quot;USER&quot;" target="&quot;CENTRAL ENTITY&quot;">
  <data key="d3">152.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The User experiences issues when the Central Entity is incorrectly selected, indicating a relationship of system design and user navigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The User's ability to access the P&amp;L MPC report is limited by their association with a Local Entity rather than the Central Entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The User's selection may inadvertently be set to the Central Entity, which can lead to potential confusion or incorrect data display."&lt;SEP&gt;"The user must be associated with the central entity to access the P&amp;L MPC report successfully."&lt;SEP&gt;"The user's inability to access the P&amp;L MPC report is influenced by their location in a local entity instead of the central entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"When the user selects the central entity incorrectly, it leads to issues in their interaction with the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The User's position outside of the Central Entity is the reason for their access issues to the P&amp;L MPC report."&lt;SEP&gt;"The user experiences issues when the selection defaults to the central entity instead of their local entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The user's lack of access relates to their affiliation with a local entity instead of the central entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The user is based in a local entity, which affects their access to reports typically available in the central entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"User may unintentionally select the central entity instead of the local entity due to interface design issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The user may mistakenly select the central entity instead of the local entity, impacting their data retrieval."&lt;SEP&gt;"The User is located in a local entity but must interface with the Central Entity to gain proper access for report presentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The user's selection of the local entity instead of the central entity has resulted in access restrictions to reporting."&lt;/|&gt;"entity selection, access restrictions"&lt;SEP&gt;"The user is not based in the central entity, which impacts their ability to access the P&amp;L MPC report."&lt;SEP&gt;"The access privileges of Users are tied to their location, specifically whether they are part of the Central Entity or a local one."&lt;SEP&gt;"The user's local entity position is contrasted with the central entity, impacting their access to reports."&lt;SEP&gt;"The user is contrasted with the Central Entity, emphasizing the selection issue in entity choice."&lt;SEP&gt;"The User interacts with the Central Entity but may face challenges when selecting the correct entity, indicating a dependence on the Central Entity for proper data retrieval."&lt;SEP&gt;"The User may unintentionally select the Central Entity instead of the Local Entity, leading to potential data mismatches."&lt;SEP&gt;"The user interacts with the central entity through the software interface, which provides broader organizational options."&lt;SEP&gt;"User's access is restricted due to their association with a Local Entity instead of the Central Entity, affecting their ability to view reports."&lt;SEP&gt;"The user should ideally interact with the central entity, but might mistakenly choose a local entity instead."&lt;SEP&gt;"The User's access to the P&amp;L MPC Report is limited because they are based in a Local Entity rather than the Central Entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The User's issues arise from the mismatch between their Local Entity and the Central Entity selected in the system."</data>
