<edge source="&quot;CENTRAL ENTITY&quot;" target="&quot;LOCAL ENTITY&quot;">
  <data key="d3">234.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Central Entity and Local Entity are related as different options in the entity dropdown that the User can choose from, impacting the outcome of data displayed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central Entity and Local Entity represent different levels of data selection affecting the User's experience and data display."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entities are distinct from the central entity and present challenges when users erroneously select the central entity instead of their local counterpart."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central entity and local entity distinction determines the level of access users have in OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity and the central entity are contrasted as options in the selection process, impacting user experience."&lt;SEP&gt;"The distinction between Central Entity and Local Entity highlights differing levels of access rights within OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity is discussed in contrast to the central entity, indicating a distinction in their roles within the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central entity operates in conjunction with local entities, providing overarching structure while local entities manage specific issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity incorrectly selected the central entity instead of the specific local entity, highlighting confusion in the entity selection process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity represents a distinct choice that contrasts with the central entity during the selection process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity is typically selected by users who are not associated with the central entity during the selection process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entities have different access rights compared to the central entity, affecting the user's ability to present the report."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entity and central entity represent different levels in the organizational structure, influencing how selection is made."&lt;SEP&gt;"The relationship between the Central Entity and Local Entity indicates a structural division that impacts report access."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Local Entity is contrasted with the Central Entity in the context of entity selection and data representation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity is contrasted with the Central Entity, indicating different levels of organizational structure and entity selection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity operates under the framework of the central entity, reflecting a hierarchical relationship in user data management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central entity serves as a contrasting entity type against which local entities are defined within the system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central entity and local entity represent different levels within the organization, influencing user access to information."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity is defined in relation to the central entity, indicating different levels of organizational structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity is often mistakenly selected instead of the central entity, indicating a confusion in user choices."&lt;SEP&gt;"The relationship between the central entity and local entity highlights the distinction in user access rights for reporting purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central entity is contrasted with the local entity in the context of user interface operations, indicating different levels of organizational hierarchy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Local Entity operates under the umbrella of the Central Entity, suggesting a hierarchical relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local entity is contrasted with the central entity, highlighting the distinctions in selection and user experience."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central entity manages data access, while local entities like EPG_Legal operate under its framework."&lt;SEP&gt;"The user might incorrectly select the Central Entity instead of their Local Entity, leading to systemic issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The relationship highlights the difference in reporting capabilities between the central entity and local entities like EPG_Legal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central entity and local entity are both organizational types relevant to user selection in the software system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Central Entity is distinct from the Local Entity, indicating a structure where reports are managed centrally but accessed locally."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central entity and local entity represent different layers of the organizational structure within the system, affecting user selection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The distinction between central and local entities is crucial for determining data access and reporting capabilities within OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Local Entity is contrasted with the Central Entity, indicating a distinction in the entity selection process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The distinction between Central Entity and Local Entity explains why the User does not have access to certain reports."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity is an alternative to Central Entity, indicating a potential conflict or misselection in the user interface."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local Entity is based on specific user selection and contrasts with Central Entity, highlighting the system's design to accommodate local variations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central entity and local entity represent different organizational structures within OneStream, influencing user access capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local entities often face restrictions that differ from central entities, affecting data access and report presentation."</data>
  <data key="d5">"access levels, entity distinction"&lt;SEP&gt;"access restrictions, organizational hierarchy"&lt;SEP&gt;"access rights, entity differences"&lt;SEP&gt;"access rights, organizational structure"&lt;SEP&gt;"contrast, selection process"&lt;SEP&gt;"data accessibility, operational structure"&lt;SEP&gt;"data hierarchy, selection issues"&lt;SEP&gt;"distinction, structure"&lt;SEP&gt;"entity differentiation, system design"&lt;SEP&gt;"entity distinction, selection process"&lt;SEP&gt;"entity hierarchy, selection contrast"&lt;SEP&gt;"hierarchical structure, data relationships"&lt;SEP&gt;"hierarchical structure, organizational levels"&lt;SEP&gt;"hierarchy, organizational structure"&lt;SEP&gt;"interface issue, selection discrepancy"&lt;SEP&gt;"local vs central, entity management"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational division, access disparity"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational hierarchy, governance"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational hierarchy, selection process"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational hierarchy, user interface"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational structure, access control"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational structure, access differences"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational structure, access hierarchy"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational structure, access levels"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational structure, access rights"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational structure, contrast"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational structure, distinction"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational structure, reporting dynamics"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational structure, selection disparity"&lt;SEP&gt;"organizational types, user selection"&lt;SEP&gt;"selection confusion, user mistake"&lt;SEP&gt;"selection contrast, organizational difference"&lt;SEP&gt;"selection error, system interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"structural relationship, management"&lt;SEP&gt;"system design, selection variability"&lt;SEP&gt;"system error, regional distinction"&lt;SEP&gt;"system issue, entity confusion"&lt;SEP&gt;"user association, organizational hierarchy"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-de22530deea07aed27df7f24440a6b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d67c1dc051ea34b153886bca7e68844</data>
</edge>
