  <data key="d3">58.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Central users and local users are part of the same organizational hierarchy, but have differing levels of access to data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users have access privileges that local users do not possess, creating a divide in data accessibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users have access to data that local users do not, highlighting a distinction in access rights."&lt;SEP&gt;"There is a clear distinction where central users have access to data, while local users do not, highlighting a divide in roles and capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users have access to relevant data, while local users do not, creating a distinction in access rights."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users have privileges that local users lack, highlighting a disparity in access capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users have the authority to grant access, differentiating them from local users who are unable to access the relevant data without permission."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central users have access to data while local users do not, highlighting a disparity in data accessibility."</data>
