  <data key="d3">108.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"A Screenshot is a common attachment included with a Support Ticket to provide visual evidence of the error encountered by the Username when using OneStream."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Screenshot is required when raising a Support Ticket to provide evidence of the encountered issue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Screenshots are often included in Support Tickets to provide visual evidence of issues users are facing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Taking a Screenshot is often a preliminary step before raising a Support Ticket to provide necessary evidence of issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The screenshot is included in the support ticket as evidence of the user's access issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Users take a screenshot to include evidence of the error when raising a support ticket to resolve access issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"A screenshot may be included in a support ticket to help illustrate the problem being reported."&lt;SEP&gt;"Users take a screenshot to substantiate their claims in the support ticket concerning issues with the OneStream system."&lt;SEP&gt;"A screenshot is often included in a support ticket to provide visual evidence of an error or issue encountered by the user."&lt;SEP&gt;"Taking a screenshot is a necessary step for users when they raise a support ticket regarding system errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The user takes a screenshot to include with the support ticket, providing evidence of the error encountered."&lt;SEP&gt;"A screenshot is often attached to a support ticket to provide visual evidence of the issues encountered."&lt;SEP&gt;"A screenshot is often included in a Support Ticket to visually communicate the issue being faced by the User."</data>
