<edge source="&quot;OKTA&quot;" target="&quot;IT DESK&quot;">
  <data key="d3">132.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"IT Desk assists users with issues related to Okta, particularly in resetting credentials and fixing login errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IT Desk manages user profiles within the Okta system for credentials and group assignments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IT desk contacts Okta to check profiles and reset credentials when users experience login issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IT desk is responsible for managing and resolving issues related to the Okta profile, which include credential resets and group assignments."&lt;SEP&gt;"IT desk interacts with Okta to manage user credentials and resolve access issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IT desk manages and resolves issues related to the Okta service, ensuring users have appropriate access and credentials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IT desk works with Okta to resolve issues related to user authentication and credentials."&lt;SEP&gt;"IT Desk uses the Okta platform to check user profiles and reset credentials for effective problem resolution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IT Desk manages and addresses issues related to the Okta authentication service for user profiles."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IT Desk supports users in managing their Okta profiles, including resetting credentials and updating group assignments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IT desk is responsible for checking the Okta profile and handling related issues like credential resets and group assignments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IT Desk checks the Okta profile as part of the process to resolve the login issue faced by the user."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IT desk interacts with Okta to manage user accounts and resolve login issues, indicating a collaborative relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IT Desk manages user profiles in Okta to resolve login issues, including resetting credentials."&lt;SEP&gt;"IT Desk checks and interacts with Okta to resolve user login issues related to credentials or group assignments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IT desk interacts with the Okta platform to resolve login issues related to user profiles and credentials."</data>
